---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../lib";
---

<Base
  title="AI code review setup"
  description="AI review on every pull request, with least-privilege permissions, spend limits and guardrails, tuned to your codebase and handed over."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Package 3</p>
  <h1>AI code review setup</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    AI review that catches real problems before a person looks, runs inside your own GitHub
    organisation, and cannot change anything it should not.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Teams whose reviewers are the bottleneck, and who want a useful first pass on every pull request.</li>
    <li>Teams already writing code with AI tools, who want the review side to keep up safely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is included</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Claude reviewing each pull request through GitHub Actions, using your own Anthropic account and key.</li>
    <li>Review rules built from a shared base and each repository's conventions, tuned over the first pull requests to keep noise low.</li>
    <li>Findings graded blocking, should-fix or nit, with nits collected into one comment.</li>
    <li>Guardrails: review is comment-only and never approves, pull requests from outside contributors never reach the model or its key, and timeouts and a monthly spend limit cap the cost.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you receive</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Review running on the repositories you choose.</li>
    <li>The review rules, documented so your team can adjust them.</li>
    <li>A handover session on tuning and costs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not included</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Model usage. Anthropic bills your own account directly, so you see and control that cost.</li>
    <li>Ongoing tuning after the handover.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="cta"><a class="button" href={href("contact/")}>Discuss AI review</a></p>
</Base>
